# Every text file gets LF, everywhere it's checked out — regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout gives
# backend/scripts/entrypoint.sh CRLF line endings, which breaks its `#!/bin/sh`
# shebang inside the Linux container it's copied into (Docker reports the script
# itself as "no such file or directory", since the interpreter path becomes
# "/bin/sh\r").
* text=auto eol=lf
